Śikṣāṣṭakam"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"subtitle":["Song 7c"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["sakhi go kemote dhoribo parāṇ","nimeṣa hoilo jugera samān"],"translation":["Oh my dear girlfriend! How will I  maintain my life? The passing of a mere moment has become like a vast age of time."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["śrāvaṇera dhārā,    ā̐khi-bariṣoy,","    śūnya bhelo dharā-tala","govinda-virahe,    prāṇa nāhi rohe,","    kemone bā̐chibo bolo"],"translation":["Tears flow from my eyes like torrents of rain in the month of Śrāvaṇa, and the face of the earth has become totally void. In separation from Govinda my life cannot go on... please, tell how I will be able to live."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["bhakativinoda,    asthira hoiyā,","    punaḥ nāmāśroya kori’","ḍāke rādhānātha,    diyā daraśana,","    prāṇa rākho, nahe mori"],"translation":["Bhakti Vinod has become very restless and again takes shelter of the holy name, calling out, “Oh Lord of Rādhā! By bestowing Your audience, please save my life! By Your mercy alone I shall not perish!”","Footnote to verse 1: *Śrīla Śrīdhar Mahārāja advised not to sing ‘sakhi go’ but ‘bandhu he’ instead.*"],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/sakhi-go-kemote","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"},{"title":"Bhakti Lalita Devi","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bhakti-lalita-devi/sakhi-go-kemote","personSlug":"bhakti-lalita-devi"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en-2022/sakhi-go-kemote-dhoribo-paran/","description":"Śrī Śikṣāṣṭakam — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Śrī Śikṣāṣṭakam. Song 7c | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-2022","slug":"sakhi-go-kemote-dhoribo-pa